goals:
- small
- retargetable
- portable (no external dependencies and minimal libc dependencies)
- complete toolchain
  - compiler & assembler
  - linker
  - interpreter (compile & load)
  - build system
  - package manager

why not:
- clang/gcc lib
  - massive
  - lacks build system & package manager
- tinycc
  - messy codebase
  - lacks optimization
  - lacks build system & package manager
- golang
  - probably closes to the end goal, but still massive
  - require external dependencies

prepare:
gcc -Wall -O3 -otic main.c

run: ./tic <arch> <code> where arch could be "e" for inideate execution
./tic a hello.c


syntax:
                                 optional
decl = <type> <name>             = <init> ; // for variable
     | <type> <name> [<size>   ] = <init> ; // for array
     | <type> <name> (<params> ) { <body> } // for call
     | struct name   {<members>}          ;
